    <p>Under the hood, every JS object has a hidden <code style="color:var(--accent-cyan)">[[Prototype]]</code> link. When you access a property, JS walks up this chain until it finds it.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Arrays inherit from <code style="color:var(--accent-cyan)">Array.prototype</code></li>
      <li>All objects ultimately inherit from <code style="color:var(--accent-purple)">Object.prototype</code></li>
